  "prefLabel": "Plc 2102.01 Arbitration",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Plc 2102.01 “Arbitration” means a procedure in which a dispute is submitted, by agreement of the parties, to a neutral or panel of neutrals who make(s) a decision on the dispute. The term includes “binding arbitration”, in which the parties are bound the decision, and “non-binding arbitration”, in which the parties are not bound by the decision.\n\nSource. #14331, eff 8-20-25, EXPIRES: 8-20-35",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/plc2100.html"
